	(text "PGP and PGN pull their own node low when bad. Each node is the +15 V rail through 220k/62k (about 3.2 V when good, under 0.3 V if its pin pulls low or the rail is missing) and lights its LED green, or red when low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4abeb73e-e0e4-50e1-9d87-5d50904fff31")
	)
	(text "-15 V GUARD: an unpowered LT3094 cannot pull PGN low. Midpoint near 0 V with both rails up, about +7.5 V with -15 V missing."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5264324b-0654-5909-933c-659b0b5c1ac5")
	)
	(text "PG_15V = the two nodes ANDed by a BAT54AW with a 470k pull-up to +3V3 (weak so it cannot lift dead nodes; 3.3 V only when both are good); it gates the amplifier REM switch and reads LOW on GPIO43 (PG_15V_N) when both rails are good."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "84cdd26a-8681-5a53-8b07-50134b7b317f")
	)
